# lastikadi.com — HTTP response headers
#
# Host mapping is a Founder decision and is NOT made in this repository, so
# nothing is deployed here. This file uses the `_headers` convention understood
# by Netlify and Cloudflare Pages; translate it to the equivalent nginx or
# Apache directives if a different host is chosen.
#
# This file states the security posture. It deliberately states NO cache
# directives: those are generated into dist/_headers by scripts/emit-dist.mjs,
# from the files that were actually emitted. One home for the policy, and the
# policy cannot fall out of step with the tree it describes.
#
# Rationale for the non-obvious entries:
#   - COEP is deliberately NOT set. It would block nothing today, but it is a
#     commitment that quietly breaks any future third-party embed, and this page
#     deliberately has none;
#   - the brand and font binaries carry recorded sha256 values in
#     assets/brand/manifest.json and assets/fonts/MANIFEST.json. That is a
#     statement about the repository, not about delivery: a manifest updates in a
#     second and a browser cache cannot be reached from here at all. It is
#     therefore recorded in the manifests and asserted by tests, and it is not
#     used as an argument for a cache lifetime;
#   - Cache-Control is absent below and generated above that line. A long
#     immutable lifetime is only truthful on a content-addressed URL, and the
#     build is what makes these URLs content-addressed. See
#     docs/CACHE-AND-DEPLOY-PLAN.md and scripts/emit-dist.mjs.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# GENERATED by scripts/emit-dist.mjs - do not edit by hand.
#
# Cache-Control lives here and nowhere else. The source `_headers` carries no
# cache directives on purpose, so there is one statement of this policy and it
# is derived from the files that were actually emitted rather than from a list
# that can drift.
#
# The invariant this file exists to hold:
#   * every path below `immutable` is content-addressed, and
#   * no path that is not content-addressed receives a long lifetime.
# A changed asset therefore gets a new URL that no cache can be holding, so an
# asset change and a claim withdrawal both take effect on the next fetch of the
# revalidated entry document - with no cache purge anywhere in the procedure.
#
# content tag: 32 bits of sha256 across 20 files
# collision probability ~5e-8; see emit-dist.mjs
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------

/assets/brand/*
  cache-control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  x-content-type-options: nosniff

/assets/css/*
  cache-control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  x-content-type-options: nosniff

/assets/fonts/*
  cache-control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  x-content-type-options: nosniff

/assets/js/*
  cache-control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  x-content-type-options: nosniff

/site.f2e64232.webmanifest
  cache-control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  x-content-type-options: nosniff

/
  cache-control: no-cache

/index.html
  cache-control: no-cache

/robots.txt
  cache-control: no-cache

/sitemap.xml
  cache-control: no-cache
